Library/Hashing/Sha2/

The Lean files of Spec/, Impl/, and Equiv/, and Spec.lean, are copied from the
directories spec/, impl/, and equiv/, and the file spec.lean, of fips-180-4-lean,
https://github.com/remix7531/fips-180-4-lean/tree/0018b08f3458553ad511e92a96336979c1e0c45a,
by remix7531, licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.
Spec/ is a literate Lean transcription of NIST FIPS 180-4.  Impl/ holds an
implementation of SHA-224, SHA-256, SHA-384, SHA-512, SHA-512/224, and
SHA-512/256 on bytes, and Equiv/ proves it equal to the transcription.  A copy
of the license is in LICENSE beside this file.

Changes: the import paths name these modules instead of `spec.*`, `impl.*`, and
`equiv.*`.  The proofs of `SHS.SHA512.H0_512_224_correct` and
`SHS.SHA512.H0_512_256_correct` use `decide +kernel` instead of `native_decide`,
so they depend on no axiom beyond `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and
`Quot.sound`.  Lean 4.34 desugars the mutable variables of a `do` block into
nested `Prod` pairs instead of `MProd`, so the tuple types `ImplVarsTuple` of
Equiv/SHA512/Compress/Impl.lean and `SpecVarsTuple` of the two
Foldl/Sequential.lean files are nested `Prod` types.  Under Lean 4.34 a
definitional check that a `match` on the round fold equals its restatement
unfolds the fold until the recursion limit, and so does the closing `rfl` of
`congr 1`.  `spec_compress_eq_seq` of the two Foldl/Sequential.lean files
therefore abstracts the fold with `generalize` before applying `hfinal`, and
`spec_compress_eq_fused` of the two Foldl/Fused.lean files uses
`congrArg (addH H)` instead of `congr 1`.  The Markdown chapters,
the README of equiv/, the logo, and the document-generation support files of
the upstream directories are omitted.
